dimensional-formula-9e2c3624.conceptual_definition:
The dimensional formula 
[S] = [Energy] \cdot [Time] = M L^2 T^{-1} 
relates a physical quantity denoted by \(S\) to its fundamental dimensions in terms of mass (M), length (L), and time (T). This particular dimensional formula corresponds to the dimension of angular momentum or action. It signifies that quantities with these dimensions are products of energy and time, or equivalently, possess the same dimensional structure as angular momentum.
